---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms governing use of The Layer Line website."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <div class="container prose-page">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Terms of Use', href: '/terms/' }]} />
    <header class="prose-page__header">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="prose-page__lead">Last updated September 1, 2026.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-page__body">
      <p>By using this site, you agree to these terms. This is a general template — have it reviewed by qualified legal counsel before relying on it for a live commercial site.</p>

      <h2>Content is informational, not professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Guides, calculators, and other content on this site are provided for general informational purposes about
        desktop 3D printing. 3D printers involve heating elements, moving parts, and materials that can be hazardous
        if mishandled. Follow your printer and filament manufacturer's own safety instructions, and use appropriate
        judgment and supervision, especially around unattended printing.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        Content is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind, express or implied. We work to keep guides
        accurate and current (see our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>), but we don't guarantee
        that any setting, calculation, or recommendation will produce a specific result on your particular
        hardware.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, The Layer Line is not liable for any damages arising from use of
        this site or reliance on its content, including damage to equipment, materials, or property.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Text, graphics, and tools on this site are owned by The Layer Line unless otherwise noted, and may not be
        republished or redistributed without permission. You're welcome to link to any page on this site.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        This site links to external resources (manufacturer documentation, community resources) for reference. We
        don't control and aren't responsible for the content or availability of external sites.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site displays advertising, including through Google AdSense. See our
        <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for how that affects data collection.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms from time to time; the date above reflects the most recent revision.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@thelayerline.com">hello@thelayerline.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
